## Root cause (measured with this worktree's .venv: transformers 5.20.0, torch 2.14.1+xpu)

jdewitt/capture.py:472 tries factories in this order: (AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoModel).
For this checkpoint:

    cfg class MiniCPMV4_7Config  model_type minicpmv4_7
    AutoModelForCausalLM._model_mapping[type(cfg)] -> KeyError   (not registered)
    AutoModel._model_mapping[type(cfg)]             -> transformers...MiniCPMV4_7Model
    transformers.MiniCPMV4_7ForConditionalGeneration exists: True
    config.json architectures = ['MiniCPMV4_7ForConditionalGeneration']

so the fallback silently loads the headless base model (lm_head UNEXPECTED in the load
report), which has no .generate. This is a loader gap in jdewitt capture, not a prep
defect in run_waves.sh and not a GPU/b70 problem: the same argv fails deterministically.

The nesting helpers already cope with a multimodal config (hidden_width / expected_layers
read config.text_config; 1024 x 24 per verification/minicpm-v47/summary.json, where this
checkpoint was previously loaded and residual-captured on the b70). Only the model class
factory is missing.

